cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Hookset: time-to-anchor as a measure of model and agent maturity"
message: If you use Hookset, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - name: eternal-roman
    alias: eternal-roman
repository-code: https://github.com/eternal-roman/hookset
url: https://github.com/eternal-roman/hookset
abstract: >-
  Hookset measures time-to-anchor (TTA), the normalized
  position of first commitment to a planted early claim,
  as a maturity metric for language models and tool-using
  agents. Longer TTA indicates more inference before
  commitment. Scoring is deterministic (lexical, optional
  log-probabilities, agent-step traces) and comparable to
  the predecessor model-testing-protocol via shared
  maturity weights.
keywords:
  - time-to-anchor
  - anchoring bias
  - LLM evaluation
  - agents
  - benchmark
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-14"
